        "original_id": "911268f7-d574-510f-bb35-c3c9f9b5e25b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Civil Defence Forces, Revolutionary United Front, National Patriotic Front of Liberia\n- People: Foday Sankoh, Charles Taylor, Joseph Momoh\n- Events: Sierra Leone Civil War\n- Places: Sierra Leone, Liberia\n- Concepts: Kamajors, Mende ethnic group\n\nFacts:\n- The Sierra Leone Civil War began on 23 March 1991 when the Revolutionary United Front intervened in Sierra Leone with support from the special forces of Charles Taylor’s National Patriotic Front of Liberia to try to overthrow the Joseph Momoh government.\n- The Sierra Leone Civil War lasted from 1991 to 2002, lasted 11 years, and caused more than 50,000 deaths.\n- The Civil Defence Forces was a paramilitary organization that fought in the Sierra Leone Civil War.\n- Much of the Civil Defence Forces was made up of the Kamajors, a group that is part of the larger Mende ethnic group.\n- Foday Saybana Sankoh, born on 17 October 1937 and died on 29 July 2003, founded and led the Revolutionary United Front during the Sierra Leone Civil War.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
